  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 56. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 勝負 — 勝つことと負けることを決める競争。\n2. 初夏 — 夏の始めごろ。\n3. 初回 — いちばん初めの回。\n4. 初期 — 物事が始まって間もない時期。\n5. 食後 — 食事をした後。\n6. 職場 — 働いて仕事をする場所。\n7. 食費 — 食べ物や食事に使うお金。\n8. 書斎 — 本を読んだり物を書いたりする部屋。\n9. 書式 — 文書を書くときの決まった形。\n10. 書籍 — 本のこと。\n11. 所蔵 — 本や作品などを持って保管していること。\n12. 所属 — ある団体や組織の一員であること。\n13. ショップ — 品物などを売る店。\n14. 書道 — 筆で文字を美しく表現することを学ぶもの。\n15. 初日 — 催しや活動などが始まる日。\n16. ショベル — 土などをすくったり掘ったりする道具。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
